\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 ## Astoria Open: System Architecture Document\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Overview\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
The Astoria Open application is an advanced conversational AI platform designed to provide a unified, natural language interface to disparate data sources. It combines structured data from traditional SQL databases with unstructured text from document libraries, presenting a synthesized, panoramic view of the subject matter to the user. While currently configured for maritime history, it is built as a generic platform adaptable to any data domain.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 ### 1. User Features\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
From an end-user's perspective, the application provides the following key features:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Natural Language Querying:
\f0\b0  Users can ask questions in plain English, eliminating the need for technical knowledge of SQL or database schemas.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Unified Data Access:
\f0\b0  The system retrieves information from both a structured SQL database and an unstructured document library (vector database) simultaneously.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Synthesized Narrative Summaries:
\f0\b0  For simple queries, the application provides a concise, AI-generated narrative that combines and summarizes the findings from all data sources.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Complex Analytical Capability:
\f0\b0  For complex or ambiguous questions, the system uses a powerful AI agent to explore the database, reason about the data, and provide a direct answer.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Transparent & Verifiable Results:
\f0\b0  Users can view the raw data tables and the exact SQL query that was generated by the AI, ensuring transparency and trust in the results.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Query History:
\f0\b0  The interface maintains a session history of all questions asked, allowing users to easily revisit previous results.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 ### 2. Architecture Components\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
The application is built on a modern, multi-LLM architecture, with each component specializing in a specific task.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Frontend UI:
\f0\b0  A responsive Single-Page Application (SPA) built with 
\f1\b React and Vite
\f0\b0 . It provides the full user experience and runs in the user's browser.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Backend Server:
\f0\b0  A high-performance 
\f1\b FastAPI
\f0\b0  application running on a 
\f1\b Gunicorn/Uvicorn
\f0\b0  server. It exposes the REST API that the frontend communicates with.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Intelligent Router:
\f0\b0  A logic layer within the backend that analyzes incoming user queries and routes them to the most appropriate tool\'97either the Direct SQL Chain or the SQL Agent.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Direct SQL Chain:
\f0\b0  The primary tool for simple, factual questions. It uses 
\f1\b Google's Gemini API
\f0\b0  to convert a natural language question directly into an efficient SQL query.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 SQL Agent:
\f0\b0  A powerful, autonomous agent also powered by 
\f1\b Google's Gemini API
\f0\b0 . It is used for complex, ambiguous, or multi-step queries that require reasoning, database exploration (e.g., checking table schemas), and self-correction.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Vector Database:
\f0\b0  A 
\f1\b PostgreSQL
\f0\b0  database supercharged with the 
\f1\b pgvector
\f0\b0  extension and hosted on 
\f1\b Supabase
\f0\b0 . It stores vector embeddings of unstructured text documents for fast semantic search.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Embeddings Model:
\f0\b0  A 
\f2\fs26 sentence-transformers
\f0\fs24  model that converts user queries and documents into numerical vectors for storage and comparison in the Vector Database.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Narrative Synthesizer:
\f0\b0  A fast 
\f1\b Groq
\f0\b0 -powered Llama 3 model responsible for the final step of the RAG pipeline: taking the structured results from the SQL query and the unstructured context from the vector search and synthesizing them into a cohesive, human-readable narrative.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 ### 3. Detailed Data Flow\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
The application's data flow intelligently adapts based on the complexity of the user's question, following one of two primary paths.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa332\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs20 \cf0 \strokec2 Simple Query Flow (e.g., "List 5 schooners")\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The user submits the query through the React UI.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The FastAPI backend receives the request at the 
\f2\fs26 /api/query
\f0\fs24  endpoint.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 
\f1\b Intelligent Router
\f0\b0  analyzes the query and identifies it as a simple, factual question.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The query is passed to the 
\f1\b Direct SQL Chain
\f0\b0 .\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The chain sends the query to the 
\f1\b Gemini API
\f0\b0 , which returns an optimized SQL string.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The backend executes the SQL against the 
\f1\b PostgreSQL Database
\f0\b0 , retrieving structured results (e.g., a list of ships).\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Simultaneously, the original user query is converted into a vector by the 
\f1\b Embeddings Model
\f0\b0 .\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 This vector is used to search the 
\f1\b Vector Database
\f0\b0  for relevant unstructured documents (e.g., historical texts about schooners).\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Both the structured SQL results and the unstructured vector context are passed to the 
\f1\b Narrative Synthesizer
\f0\b0 .\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 
\f1\b Groq LLM
\f0\b0  generates a final narrative summary.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	11	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The backend packages the narrative, the raw SQL results, and the generated SQL into a single JSON response and sends it back to the React UI for display.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa332\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs20 \cf0 \strokec2 Complex Query Flow (e.g., "Analyze the most common engine types")\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The user submits the query through the React UI.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The FastAPI backend receives the request.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 
\f1\b Intelligent Router
\f0\b0  analyzes the query and identifies it as complex and analytical.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The query is passed to the 
\f1\b SQL Agent
\f0\b0 .\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 
\f1\b SQL Agent (powered by Gemini)
\f0\b0  begins a reasoning process. It might first use a tool to list the database tables, then another tool to inspect the schema of the 
\f2\fs26 vessels
\f0\fs24  table to understand its columns.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Based on this exploration, the Agent formulates and executes one or more SQL queries against the 
\f1\b PostgreSQL Database
\f0\b0 .\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 After analyzing the results, the Agent formulates a final, text-based answer to the user's question.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The backend packages the agent's final answer into a JSON response and sends it back to the React UI for display.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 ### 4. The Platform Architecture\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
This application was designed not just as a tool for maritime history but as a reusable 
\f1\b platform
\f0\b0  for creating a natural language interface for any domain with both structured and unstructured data. The core architecture is completely data-agnostic.  Open source according to Apache 2.0 license. \
To adapt this platform to a new context (e.g., financial analysis, medical records, or product inventories), only the data and the AI's "persona" need to be changed:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Data:
\f0\b0  Connect the system to a new SQL database and load new, domain-specific documents into the vector database.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Prompts:
\f0\b0  Update the system prompts for the agent and the narrative synthesizer to reflect the new domain (e.g., changing the persona from a "maritime historian" to a "financial analyst").\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 The underlying code\'97the FastAPI server, the React UI, the intelligent router, and the entire data flow logic\'97would remain unchanged. This makes the system a powerful and flexible platform for providing a single, panoramic, and conversational view of any subject matter.\
}